<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Centre and radius of a constant angle arc</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>\(A\) and \(B\) are \({@c@}\) cm apart. The locus of a point \(P\) on one side of \(AB\) with angle \(APB = {@th@}^{\circ}\) is an arc of a circle with centre \(O\).</p><div style="text-align:center;" role="img" aria-label="Segment AB with midpoint M and its perpendicular bisector drawn dashed. The centre O of the arc is on the bisector, on the same side as the arc. The arc of the circle with centre O runs from A to B, and P on it has angle APB = {#th#} degrees. The diagram is not to scale.">
[[jsxgraph width="320px" height="260px"]]
(function () {
  var th = {#th#} * Math.PI / 180, oy = 3 / Math.tan(th), R = 3 / Math.sin(th), top = oy + R + 1;
  var w = Math.max(R + 1, (top + 1.5) * 320 / 260 / 2);
  var b = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {boundingbox: [-w, top, w, -1.5], keepAspectRatio: true, axis: false, grid: false,
    showNavigation: false, showCopyright: false, pan: {enabled: false}, zoom: {enabled: false}});
  var A = b.create('point', [-3, 0], {name: 'A', fixed: true, size: 2, color: '#000000', label: {offset: [-14, -10]}});
  var B = b.create('point', [3, 0], {name: 'B', fixed: true, size: 2, color: '#000000', label: {offset: [6, -10]}});
  var M = b.create('point', [0, 0], {name: 'M', fixed: true, size: 1.5, color: '#000000', label: {offset: [4, -12]}});
  var O = b.create('point', [0, oy], {name: 'O', fixed: true, size: 2, color: '#1f4e9c', label: {offset: [6, 0]}});
  var P = b.create('point', [0, oy + R], {name: 'P', fixed: true, size: 2, color: '#b00000', label: {offset: [4, 8]}});
  b.create('segment', [A, B], {strokeColor: '#000000', strokeWidth: 2, fixed: true, highlight: false});
  b.create('segment', [[0, -1.2], [0, top - 0.3]], {strokeColor: '#555555', strokeWidth: 1, dash: 2, fixed: true, highlight: false});
  b.create('arc', [O, B, A], {strokeColor: '#1f4e9c', strokeWidth: 2, fixed: true, highlight: false});
  b.create('segment', [P, A], {strokeColor: '#b00000', strokeWidth: 1, fixed: true, highlight: false});
  b.create('segment', [P, B], {strokeColor: '#b00000', strokeWidth: 1, fixed: true, highlight: false});
  b.create('nonreflexangle', [A, P, B], {radius: 0.8, name: '{#th#}°', fixed: true, fillOpacity: 0.15, label: {fontSize: 12}});
})();
[[/jsxgraph]]
</div><p>(a)</p><div>Angle \(AOB = \) [[input:ans1]] \(^\circ\) [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b)</p><div>Angle \(OAB = \) [[input:ans2]] \(^\circ\) [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><p>(c) Find the radius of the arc, correct to 1 decimal place.</p><div>[[input:ans3]] cm [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) The angle at the centre is twice the angle at the circumference: angle \(AOB = 2 \times {@th@}^{\circ} = {@2*th@}^{\circ}\).</p><p>(b) \(OA = OB\) (radii), so triangle \(OAB\) is isosceles: angle \(OAB = \dfrac{180^{\circ} - {@2*th@}^{\circ}}{2} = {@90-th@}^{\circ}\), that is \(90^{\circ} - {@th@}^{\circ}\). This is the angle used to construct the centre.</p><p>(c) Let \(M\) be the midpoint of \(AB\). In the right-angled triangle \(OMA\), \(AM = {@exd(c/2)@}\) cm and angle \(AOM = {@th@}^{\circ}\) (half of angle \(AOB\)). So \(OA = \dfrac{AM}{\sin {@th@}^{\circ}} = \dfrac{ {@exd(c/2)@} }{\sin {@th@}^{\circ}} = {@dispdp(float(floor(10^2*(rr)+1/2)/10^2),2)@}\), so the radius is \({@dispdp(float(floor(10^1*(rr)+1/2)/10^1),1)@}\) cm to 1 decimal place.</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[/* exd: shortest exact decimal display of a terminating value (up to 3 d.p.) */
exd(v) := if integerp(v) then v else if integerp(10*v) then dispdp(float(v),1) else if integerp(100*v) then dispdp(float(v),2) else dispdp(float(v),3);
/* Design: centre and radius of a constant angle arc. Allowed (c, theta): theta 40, 45, 50, 60, 80 are excluded for every c (45 and 60 make a diagnostic equal the answer; 40, 50, 80 put diagnostics too close together); theta 30 omits c = 7 (the chapter's exercise); theta 75 omits 4 and 5 (diagnostics too close). Source: original. */
thl: [30,35,55,65,70,75];
cl: [[4,5,6,8,9,10,11,12],[4,5,6,7,8,9,10,11,12],[4,5,6,7,8,9,10,11,12],[4,5,6,7,8,9,10,11,12],[4,5,6,7,8,9,10,11,12],[6,7,8,9,10,11,12]];
j: 1+rand(6);
th: thl[j];
c: rand(cl[j]);
sn: sin(th*%pi/180);
rr: c/(2*sn);
/* diagnostics (c): angle 2 theta used in triangle OMA; half of AB; OM; AB not halved */
d1: c/(2*sin(2*th*%pi/180));
d2: c/2;
d3: (c/2)/tan(th*%pi/180);
d4: c/sn;]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
